+# US-06: Model catalogue
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Epic | WBMME-2 Model Training & Selection |
+| Requirement | MLE-F-007 |
+| Points / sprint | 3 / Sprint 1 |
+| Owner | Varnika (Member 2) |
+| SAD component | Model Selection & Training |
+| Design reference | DS-Model-01 |
+
+**Story.** As a Data Scientist or Student I want to choose a model from a fixed catalogue so that I can compare algorithms without writing code.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (from SRS 4.3 and Table 4.3-1)
+
+- [x] The catalogue has exactly four classification models: Logistic Regression, k-Nearest Neighbours, Decision Tree, Random Forest.
+- [x] Each model exposes its default parameters and permitted ranges.
+- [x] A user selects exactly one model per run (the model is chosen by key, validated against the catalogue in US-08).
+- [x] The catalogue is fixed: no user-supplied model or algorithm is accepted (MLE-SR-004 / SAD risk R3).
+- [x] `GET /api/models` returns the catalogue to a logged-in user and 401 to anyone else.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `training/catalogue.py` | `ModelSpec`, `ParamSpec`, the four models, `build_estimator()` |
+| `training/views.py`, `training/urls.py` | `GET /api/models` |
+| `training/http.py` | JSON helpers and `api_login_required` |
+| `training/tests/test_catalogue.py`, `test_api_models.py` | 23 tests, tagged with `req("MLE-F-007")` |
+| `member2_dev/` | Stand-alone dev harness (settings, URLs, dev login) so the app runs before the team skeleton (US-14) is merged |
+
+## How to demo
+
+```bash
+python member2_dev/manage.py migrate
+python member2_dev/manage.py createsuperuser --username demo
+python member2_dev/manage.py runserver
+# in a second terminal
+curl -c jar -X POST localhost:8000/dev/login -d '{"username":"demo","password":"<password>"}'
+curl -b jar localhost:8000/api/models
+```
+
+## Test
+
+```bash
+python -m pytest -c member2_dev/pytest.ini
+```
